      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I'll read the original test and the CUT source to understand what needs to be improved.Now I understand the test. It verifies that when a `TimedSemaphore` is created with limit `0` (`NO_LIMIT`), both `tryAcquire()` and `acquire()` always pass (because the \"no limit\" mode lets all callers through), incrementing the internal counter to 2. Thus `getAvailablePermits()` returns `0 - 2 = -2`.\n\nLet me write the improved, more understandable version.The improved test compiles successfully (`COMPILE_OK`). The refactored version renames the variable to `semaphore` for clarity, replaces the magic literal `0` with `TimedSemaphore.NO_LIMIT`, and adds a concise comment explaining why both acquires succeed and why `getAvailablePermits()` returns `-2`."
    }
